We use a shared turn variable that allows only one thread at a time to enter the 
critical section. Every thread has a unique ID (0, 1, 2, ... N−1). 
Only the thread whose ID matches the current turn value is allowed to enter the 
critical section.

Once done, it updates the turn to the next thread.
How It Works

    Each thread waits until turn == id.
    When it's their turn:
        The thread enters the critical section.
        It updates turn = (turn + 1) % total_threads.

    This process continues until all threads finish.

